# Spot, Felis catus: "Whenever Spot or another nontoken legendary permanent you control enters, create a Food token." A token
# copy of Spot made by Replicate is Spot itself entering, so it triggers although it is a token (CR 603.6a); the original Spot
# does not trigger for it, being another permanent that is a token. Two Foods are made in all: one for each Spot entering.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Spot, Felis catus
Repudiate // Replicate
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Spot, Felis catus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Repudiate // Replicate.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Spot, Felis catus; Ability: Replicate)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Food Token#1.Types = Artifact
Bot1.Battlefield.Food Token#2.Types = Artifact
Bot1.Battlefield.Food Token#3 = (absent)
